{"status":"qualified","message":"Selected from independently reviewed source explanations. Interpretations are labeled separately; each reference identifies its publisher and source.","answer_mode":"cloud_reviewed_composition","reason_code":"none","claims":[{"id":"U01","text":"The location-based method considers average emission factors for the electricity grids that provide electricity. The market-based method considers the contractual arrangements under which an organization procures power from specific sources, such as renewable energy. These are accounting perspectives; this explanation does not determine that a particular purchase or instrument qualifies.","evidence_ids":["S01"],"qualifications":["This guidance explains U.S. grid-delivered purchased electricity; it does not determine a company's legal duties."]},{"id":"U02","text":"EPA’s December 2023 guide recommends that organizations quantify and report both location-based and market-based scope 2 totals in their GHG inventory. Both results should be clearly labeled with the method used. This is the guide’s reporting recommendation; the preview does not determine a particular company’s legal reporting obligations.","evidence_ids":["S01","S02"],"qualifications":["This guidance explains U.S. grid-delivered purchased electricity; it does not determine a company's legal duties.","EPA's reporting recommendation is not a universal legal obligation."]},{"id":"U03","text":"Reporting the two results with their method labels presents the grid-average perspective and the contractual procurement perspective separately. This is an explanation of what those two labeled results communicate, not a statement of EPA’s policy motive or a universal legal requirement.","evidence_ids":["S01","S02"],"qualifications":["This guidance explains U.S. grid-delivered purchased electricity; it does not determine a company's legal duties.","EPA's reporting recommendation is not a universal legal obligation."]}],"evidence":[{"id":"S01","source_id":"epa-electricity-2023","locator":"PDF page 4 / printed page 1","excerpt":"The GHG Protocol Scope 2 Guidance provides a comprehensive discussion of issues related to quantification and reporting of scope 2 emissions, and organizations are encouraged to consult that guidance. This document is aligned with the principles and methodologies defined in the GHG Protocol Scope 2 Guidance. However, it does not attempt to address all scope 2 issues. Guidance for quantifying two scope 2 emissions totals, using a location-based method and a market-based method, is included in this document. The organization should quantify and report both totals in its GHG inventory. The location-based method considers average emission factors for the electricity grids that provide electricity. The market- based method considers contractual arrangements under which the organization procures power from specific sources, such as renewable energy."},{"id":"S02","source_id":"epa-electricity-2023","locator":"PDF page 9 / printed page 6","excerpt":"Organizations should calculate and report scope 2 emissions using two methods: one using location-based emission factors, and one using market-based emission factors. Both results should be clearly labeled according to the method used."}],"sources":[{"id":"epa-electricity-2023","title":"Greenhouse Gas Inventory Guidance: Indirect Emissions from Purchased Electricity","version":"December 2023","status":"published_guidance","canonical_url":"https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2020-12/documents/electricityemissions.pdf"}],"missing_context":[],"scope_gaps":[],"release":{"id":"scope2-website","version":"1","sha256":"38f91ceac7aab790cb6faf98d39d8e0c5f2eb734f6a5763d51b6bf6ef7afa43f"},"provider":{"mode":"live","model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5"},"retrieval":{"mode":"cloud","store":"Supabase","search":"Pinecone","build_id":"63f0190c-9694-46db-9ea8-85445a80f6be","release_sha256":"38f91ceac7aab790cb6faf98d39d8e0c5f2eb734f6a5763d51b6bf6ef7afa43f","candidate_ids":["S04","S07","S01","S15","S16","S12","S03","S14","S06","S18"],"selected_ids":["S01","S02"],"checked_at":"2026-09-11T19:18:15.734Z"},"composition":{"catalog_id":"scope2-website-answer-units","version":"3-epa-acquisition","sha256":"97b2c4e0f4121c1d2ea7fa33d569f53344193f12a80e9d1349577c3a86e17e50","units":[{"id":"U01","title":"Two accounting perspectives","type":"source_summary"},{"id":"U02","title":"Reporting the two results","type":"source_summary"},{"id":"U03","title":"What separate results show","type":"reviewed_interpretation"}],"wording":"reviewed_verbatim"},"correction_attempted":false,"correction_kind":null}